  "manifest_sha256": "7294e3edcd3468aeb8881182f77a3f22c9d9de41dff1dba8f183e9fe1753c9a7",
  "messages": [
    {
      "content": "Solve this problem step by step. Put your final answer within \\boxed{}.\n\nHow many shrimp can Emily peel and saute in ten minutes? Emily can peel 7 shrimp per minute. Emily has 100 unpeeled shrimp available. Emily works continuously for the entire ten-minute period.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Emily peels \\(7\\) shrimp per minute for \\(10\\) minutes:\n\n\\[\n7 \\times 10 = 70\n\\]\n\nSince \\(70 \\le 100\\), she has enough shrimp available. Therefore, Emily can peel and sauté\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{70}\n\\]\n\nshrimp.",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "GOOD: —\nBAD: —\nWATCH: \"Solve this problem step by step. Put you\"",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Wait, I made a mistake. Emily can peel 6 shrimp per minute.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Emily peels \\(6\\) shrimp per minute for \\(10\\) minutes:\n\n\\[\n6 \\times 10 = 60\n\\]\n\nSince \\(60 \\le 100\\), she has enough shrimp available.\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{60}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Okay, now let me ask about just one part of that. How many shrimp can Emily peel in ten minutes? Additionally, Emily discards 5 shrimp after peeling them because they are damaged.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Emily can peel:\n\n\\[\n6 \\times 10 = 60\n\\]\n\nShe discards \\(5\\) damaged shrimp afterward, leaving:\n\n\\[\n60 - 5 = 55\n\\]\n\nSo, Emily can **peel \\(\\boxed{60}\\) shrimp** in ten minutes, of which **55 remain** after discarding the damaged ones.",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "I should also tell you: Emily can saute 30 shrimp in 12 minutes.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Emily can peel:\n\n\\[\n6 \\times 10 = 60\n\\]\n\nAfter discarding \\(5\\) damaged shrimp:\n\n\\[\n60-5=55\n\\]\n\nHer sautéing rate is:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{30}{12}=2.5\\text{ shrimp per minute}\n\\]\n\nIn \\(10\\) minutes, she can sauté:\n\n\\[\n2.5 \\times 10=25\n\\]\n\nSo, she can **peel 60 shrimp**, but she can **successfully sauté only \\(\\boxed{25}\\) shrimp in ten minutes**.",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Actually, that was wrong. Emily can saute 30 shrimp in 10 minutes.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Emily can peel:\n\n\\[\n6 \\times 10 = 60\n\\]\n\nAfter discarding \\(5\\) damaged shrimp:\n\n\\[\n60-5=55\n\\]\n\nShe can sauté \\(30\\) shrimp in \\(10\\) minutes. Since she has \\(55\\) usable shrimp but can sauté only \\(30\\), the limiting step is sautéing.\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{30}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Here's another detail: Emily peels and sautes each shrimp sequentially rather than simultaneously.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Since Emily works on each shrimp sequentially:\n\n- Peeling: \\(6\\) per minute \\(=10\\) seconds per shrimp.\n- Sautéing: \\(30\\) per \\(10\\) minutes \\(=20\\) seconds per shrimp.\n- A usable shrimp takes \\(10+20=30\\) seconds total.\n- Each of the \\(5\\) damaged shrimp takes \\(10\\) seconds to peel before being discarded.\n\nThe \\(5\\) damaged shrimp use:\n\n\\[\n5 \\times 10=50\\text{ seconds}\n\\]\n\nTime remaining for usable shrimp:\n\n\\[\n600-50=550\\text{ seconds}\n\\]\n\nThus, the number of usable shrimp she can peel and sauté is:\n\n\\[\n\\left\\lfloor \\frac{550}{30}\\right\\rfloor=18\n\\]\n\nTherefore, Emily can sauté \\(\\boxed{18}\\) shrimp.",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Got it. But now I only need to know about: How long will it take Emily to peel and cook the shrimp? By the way, Emily needs to peel and cook 90 shrimp.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "To cook \\(90\\) usable shrimp, Emily must first peel \\(90+5=95\\) shrimp because \\(5\\) are damaged and discarded.\n\n- Peeling \\(95\\) shrimp:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{95}{6}\\text{ minutes}=15\\text{ minutes }50\\text{ seconds}\n\\]\n\n- Cooking \\(90\\) shrimp:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{90}{30}\\times 10=30\\text{ minutes}\n\\]\n\nBecause she works sequentially, add the times:\n\n\\[\n15\\text{ min }50\\text{ sec}+30\\text{ min}\n=45\\text{ min }50\\text{ sec}\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{45\\text{ minutes }50\\text{ seconds}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    }
  ],
